  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nWith high pressure in control, clear skies, and calm winds,\ntonight will be another cool night. Lows are expected to be in\nthe mid 30s to mid 40s. Patchy frost will be possible in\nnorthern Oneida County and the usual colder spots, but coverage\nis not expected to be widespread enough for Frost Advisories.\n\nFriday will be a similar day compared to today with highs in the\nmid 60s to lower 70s. Some clouds may sneak in from an\napproaching coastal low for the Poconos-Catskills, but otherwise\nit will be another mostly sunny day. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nTrends continue for the above mentioned coastal low pressure\nsystem to track a bit farther to the west and even begin to\nretrograde into the area by Sunday. As a result, rain chances\nwere significantly expanded westward with the afternoon forecast\npackage. The heavier rain should remain east of the region, but\nsome locally moderate rainfall will be possible on Sunday as the\nlow retrogrades. Winds look to be breezy Saturday and Sunday \nwith northerly winds of 15 to 20 mph and gusts up to 30 mph.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 3... \n\nAs the coastal low begins to occlude and move out-to-sea Sunday\nnight into Monday, a general drying trend will be present. That\nbeing said, cannot rule out a few lingering rain showers,\nespecially Monday morning. High pressure then moves into the\nregion Monday night through Wednesday. A shortwave may then\nbring some scattered showers on Thursday.",
